# Ebb — State of Record

The ideal state this fleet is iterating toward, what has been established, and what was decided along the way. Written at install from the principal's answer; maintained by the commander. The grammar is specified in `INTENT.md`.

## Goal

Principal said "A public tide-table API that answers correctly for any UK coastal station, and a daily ingest that keeps it current without human attention" in the install interview at 2026-08-20.

Goal evolutions are appended here the same way: verbatim words, attribution, and date. They supersede without erasing the earlier goal.

## Claims

Established facts, each dated, evidence-citing, and falsifier-naming. Evidence must live where `wheelhouse/GRAPH.md` says evidence lives. A claim without evidence is a hope; a claim without a falsifier is not yet sharp enough to carry the project.

<!--
Empty at install, and deliberately so. An ISA with fabricated claims is worse
than an empty one, because the next reader treats it as authoritative.

When a claim is pending, keep it visibly pending instead of promoting it:
- PENDING: <claim under test>. Evidence owed: <artifact or observation>, to land at <bead comment or committed path>. Falsifier: <what would disprove it>.
-->

## Anti-claims

What this fleet is explicitly NOT doing, so nobody re-proposes it every month.

- Not building a UI. The API is the product.

## Decisions

Principal direction lands here before, or in the same breath as, the beads implementing it are dispatched. The decision entry is what those beads trace to.

| Date | Decision | Why / Trace |
|---|---|---|
| 2026-08-20 | Principal said in the illustrative install interview: "the whole point of the Wheelhouse and the mandate is to create work and to do work, not to ask if you can create work, ask if you can start work, and ask if the work can be declared done." | Autonomy mandate recorded in `CLAUDE.md` and `wheelhouse/INTEGRATOR.md`; the fleet takes work all the way except for reserved actions and genuine product-intent forks. |
